1
00:02:04,210 --> 00:02:08,690
No living creature was hurt during
the production of this show.

2
00:02:13,329 --> 00:02:17,439
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:54,745 --> 00:02:56,445
Faster!

4
00:02:56,796 --> 00:02:59,996
We must arrive at Bilecik Castle at once!

5
00:03:04,304 --> 00:03:06,904
Guards!
Look sharp!

6
00:03:25,787 --> 00:03:26,737
Alps!

7
00:03:28,052 --> 00:03:29,512
They'll be here soon.

8
00:03:31,885 --> 00:03:33,655
We will uprise!

9
00:03:37,926 --> 00:03:39,676
Now it is time to massacre!

10
00:03:40,867 --> 00:03:43,137
We are going to appropriate all the goods!

11
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:46,270
No enemy shall remain alive!

12
00:03:46,577 --> 00:03:48,867
As you command, my Bey!

13
00:03:50,134 --> 00:03:51,844
Go!

14
00:04:45,650 --> 00:04:47,720
Defend!

15
00:04:51,562 --> 00:04:53,752
Protect the caravan!

16
00:04:55,342 --> 00:04:57,142
God is with us!

17
00:05:04,614 --> 00:05:07,384
Allahu Aqbar
(Allah is the greatest)

18
00:05:07,769 --> 00:05:09,009
Allahu Aqbar
(Allah is the greatest)

19
00:07:01,569 --> 00:07:03,099
Feodor!

20
00:07:03,857 --> 00:07:05,857
If God is with you...

21
00:07:07,207 --> 00:07:10,657
...why are you running like a jackal
running away from a lion?

22
00:07:11,075 --> 00:07:13,135
Confront me!

23
00:07:13,175 --> 00:07:14,695
Come on!

24
00:07:48,033 --> 00:07:51,183
Hurry!
Hurry up, brothers!

25
00:08:19,443 --> 00:08:22,463
I have been stabbed on my shoulder
so many times that...

26
00:08:22,895 --> 00:08:24,805
I don't feel it anymore, Osman.

27
00:08:30,268 --> 00:08:34,788
Your head... You will feel it when
I cut your head.

28
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,419
Three days ago.

29
00:08:44,171 --> 00:08:45,885
Bilecik Castle

30
00:08:45,885 --> 00:08:50,765
Priest Gregor and his friend Andreas
are not in their rooms.

31
00:08:52,536 --> 00:08:55,906
So, where are they, Feodor?

32
00:08:58,625 --> 00:09:01,465
It seems they left willingly.

33
00:09:06,351 --> 00:09:11,241
What do you think?
Do you agree with your commander?

34
00:09:16,167 --> 00:09:18,167
Yes sir.

35
00:09:26,284 --> 00:09:28,224
Take him out!

36
00:09:29,935 --> 00:09:31,295
Now!

37
00:09:35,403 --> 00:09:37,203
You stay, Feodor!

38
00:09:39,683 --> 00:09:45,773
It was really weird that Osman gave up on
Gregor without any resistance.

39
00:09:45,857 --> 00:09:48,497
Now I get it, he set up a game.

40
00:09:49,346 --> 00:09:51,636
So, what about Gregor?

41
00:09:55,512 --> 00:09:59,822
Why did he go back to Osman with
his own will?

42
00:10:00,727 --> 00:10:02,307
I don't know, sir.

43
00:10:02,350 --> 00:10:05,401
Do not interrupt me while I am
thinking out loud, Feodor!

44
00:10:05,401 --> 00:10:07,401
You should have already learned that!

45
00:10:13,607 --> 00:10:15,487
Dear Gregor...

46
00:10:16,543 --> 00:10:20,263
...let's see what is the reason that
you went back to Osman.

47
00:11:41,612 --> 00:11:45,222
Hey Passanger!
Where is your destination?

48
00:11:45,371 --> 00:11:47,481
Kizil Elma.

49
00:11:50,977 --> 00:11:52,547
Osman Bey.

50
00:11:54,883 --> 00:11:56,383
The Priest...

51
00:11:56,638 --> 00:11:59,538
The Priest run away with something
more precious than himself!

52
00:12:11,640 --> 00:12:15,750
You own the most precious
sacred of the Christian world.

53
00:12:17,195 --> 00:12:19,955
What does make it so precious?

54
00:12:21,530 --> 00:12:26,960
What you are holding in your hand
may cause a new Crusades.

55
00:12:30,963 --> 00:12:34,423
A piece of the shroud
that Jesus was crucified.

56
00:12:37,985 --> 00:12:44,445
They believe that Jesus' blood dripped
on this shroud.

57
00:12:48,133 --> 00:12:50,925
This news is all over Constantinople.

58
00:12:50,925 --> 00:12:52,875
The Emperor got mad.

59
00:12:52,974 --> 00:12:55,874
This news was delivered to all the lords.

60
00:12:57,832 --> 00:13:01,512
They will unite and attack you Osman Bey.

61
00:13:03,117 --> 00:13:05,397
You should be careful, Osman Bey.

62
00:13:05,450 --> 00:13:07,800
They may attack anytime.

63
00:13:12,977 --> 00:13:14,637
What a beautiful justice!

64
00:13:15,701 --> 00:13:18,611
Osman Bey holds their most precious...

65
00:13:20,514 --> 00:13:22,324
And they would call me devil.

66
00:13:25,338 --> 00:13:29,558
You say all the Christians unite against
me for this.

67
00:13:31,823 --> 00:13:36,963
What if I make my move first and gain the
support of Christian community?

68
00:13:38,653 --> 00:13:41,623
This would be a very dangerous move,
Osman Bey.

69
00:13:42,691 --> 00:13:45,491
Only the brave can manage difficulty.

70
00:13:49,189 --> 00:13:52,329
You are my eyes and ears.

71
00:13:52,989 --> 00:13:57,459
If you have new news, let me know.

72
00:13:58,500 --> 00:14:00,310
As you command, Osman Bey.

73
00:14:02,029 --> 00:14:04,359
Now it's my time to set up a game.

74
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:22,625
Harmankaya Castle.

75
00:14:24,922 --> 00:14:27,242
Rogatus knows what he is doing.

76
00:14:30,812 --> 00:14:33,792
He took Turgut from me by using
Catalans.

77
00:14:36,950 --> 00:14:40,080
He took him from me and gave him to Osman.

78
00:14:41,654 --> 00:14:44,074
In return of what?

79
00:14:45,429 --> 00:14:48,469
In return of Priest Gregor.

80
00:14:51,573 --> 00:14:54,993
My predicts are always true!

81
00:14:57,387 --> 00:15:00,398
Where was that Priest we were
looking for?

82
00:15:00,398 --> 00:15:02,998
In Osman's hands.

83
00:15:03,222 --> 00:15:04,842
I told you.

84
00:15:07,052 --> 00:15:08,492
Kosses.

85
00:15:10,610 --> 00:15:13,330
You didn't know that, did you?

86
00:15:15,409 --> 00:15:22,129
Because if you knew, it'd be inevitable
that you'd use Turgut with Rogatus.

87
00:15:23,846 --> 00:15:27,176
You wouldn't hide such a swap from me.

88
00:15:27,330 --> 00:15:29,050
Am I right?

89
00:15:29,050 --> 00:15:31,550
We are on the same side, Nicola.

90
00:15:32,185 --> 00:15:34,795
Why would I hide something like this?

91
00:15:35,618 --> 00:15:38,808
Caesar and Brutus.

92
00:15:40,623 --> 00:15:43,663
They were on the same side too, Kosses.

93
00:15:47,939 --> 00:15:51,929
That you suspect us is heartbreaking,
dear Nicola.

94
00:15:53,883 --> 00:15:59,133
Our only aim was to put your gift
in his place.

95
00:16:00,338 --> 00:16:08,138
Besides, Rogatus gave Turgut, whom you fight
to capture, to Osman, your biggest enemy.

96
00:16:10,864 --> 00:16:15,584
All the self sacrifice you committed for
me has been wasted.

97
00:16:16,193 --> 00:16:20,433
What Rogatus did
cannot remain unpenalized.

98
00:16:22,003 --> 00:16:26,913
The penalty will be heavy.

99
00:16:31,376 --> 00:16:36,546
I'll leave him a scar
that he won't forget.

100
00:16:50,554 --> 00:16:53,154
You say it may cause Crusades, Osman Bey!

101
00:16:53,581 --> 00:16:56,051
Can we take that?

102
00:16:57,314 --> 00:17:03,214
We must take that risk so that our
children don't experience the same, brother.

103
00:17:05,641 --> 00:17:08,711
Their aim is neither the Priest
nor the shroud.

104
00:17:09,119 --> 00:17:12,520
All they want is to banish us.

105
00:17:14,636 --> 00:17:17,856
They want to prevent us from
having our homeland here.

106
00:17:20,101 --> 00:17:23,781
My Sheik father would say
"every situation is under Lord's control"

107
00:17:25,061 --> 00:17:29,522
If Christians are able to attack, we are
able to dispel.

108
00:17:30,895 --> 00:17:33,088
Eyvallah (of course)

109
00:17:33,088 --> 00:17:34,928
Faith comes first, my Bey.

110
00:17:36,367 --> 00:17:39,737
We have religious warriors
to fight off their army.

111
00:17:41,475 --> 00:17:43,965
Thank Allah, we have.

112
00:17:47,020 --> 00:17:48,280
My intention is...

113
00:17:50,090 --> 00:17:53,960
that we may conquer the castles, the towns
from inside...

114
00:17:54,330 --> 00:17:58,790
with the help of the Priest Gregor.

115
00:18:01,456 --> 00:18:04,806
We are going to obtain the support of
non-Muslims.

116
00:18:05,580 --> 00:18:09,180
We will do that with the help of
Priest Gregor.

117
00:18:11,334 --> 00:18:15,284
Those Lords will come here!

118
00:18:15,876 --> 00:18:17,751
They will knee!

119
00:18:17,751 --> 00:18:21,881
They will beg!
They will see that...

120
00:18:22,145 --> 00:18:25,245
Their heart is in our hand.

121
00:18:25,815 --> 00:18:28,245
We are going to rip it out when we want!

122
00:18:29,823 --> 00:18:33,203
My Bey, we should start gaining their
support then.

123
00:18:33,363 --> 00:18:35,283
Let the Priest arrive in Sogut.

124
00:18:36,136 --> 00:18:39,036
He must have just got out.
He'll try again.

125
00:18:39,674 --> 00:18:43,314
That's what we want, Malhun.

126
00:18:49,872 --> 00:18:54,872
My Bey, we are going to Sogut
with Malhun Hatun for the rugs.

127
00:19:00,291 --> 00:19:02,031
Eyvallah.

128
00:19:02,555 --> 00:19:04,725
Eyvallah(okay) Hatuns.

129
00:19:14,654 --> 00:19:16,764
Bilecik Castle.

130
00:19:18,540 --> 00:19:20,520
Does he not trust me at all?

131
00:19:23,894 --> 00:19:27,824
There is only one way to learn it all.
What was that old man's name?

132
00:19:28,118 --> 00:19:30,468
- The one in the church in Sogut.
- Yun.

133
00:19:30,468 --> 00:19:31,618
Hah, Yun.

134
00:19:32,486 --> 00:19:37,316
Find Yun, tell him to learn the truth from
Gregor.

135
00:19:39,062 --> 00:19:42,232
Stop. Wait.
There's one more thing.

136
00:19:44,081 --> 00:19:49,601
Inform the Lords in Bithynia. I will be waiting
for them tomorrow, in my castle.

137
00:19:49,901 --> 00:19:51,821
Kosses included.

138
00:19:52,395 --> 00:19:54,075
As you command.

139
00:19:59,779 --> 00:20:02,269
Harmankaya Castle.

140
00:20:22,455 --> 00:20:23,705
Are you alright?

141
00:20:24,716 --> 00:20:27,110
Will you help me stand up, brother?

142
00:20:27,110 --> 00:20:29,850
Of course.
Did I hurt you?

143
00:20:33,312 --> 00:20:35,792
You should not have
underestimated me, brother.

144
00:20:38,121 --> 00:20:43,031
You are right. No Palailogos
should be underestimated.

145
00:20:49,266 --> 00:20:50,636
My lord.

146
00:20:52,517 --> 00:20:54,466
There is important news
from Bilecik.

147
00:20:54,466 --> 00:20:56,296
Speak.

148
00:20:56,865 --> 00:21:00,645
Lord Rogatus invites all lords
for tomorrow.

149
00:21:05,035 --> 00:21:07,475
He took Priest Gregor.

150
00:21:07,747 --> 00:21:12,177
He will demonstrate his
power to all of us.

151
00:21:13,499 --> 00:21:14,989
He can't, my lord.

152
00:21:15,682 --> 00:21:17,892
The other news is about this.

153
00:21:19,267 --> 00:21:24,937
Everyone is talking about how Gregor
escaped Bilecik to return Osman.

154
00:21:30,044 --> 00:21:31,714
To Osman?

155
00:21:33,184 --> 00:21:35,504
By his own will?

156
00:21:42,682 --> 00:21:46,392
Now, I'm interested in his invitation.

157
00:21:46,739 --> 00:21:48,519
What should we do?

158
00:21:50,402 --> 00:21:53,772
We'll go and see what he
has to say.

159
00:21:55,105 --> 00:21:57,075
But firstly...

160
00:21:58,280 --> 00:22:00,710
I need to see Osman.

161
00:22:02,560 --> 00:22:04,790
Will you ask for Gregor, brother?

162
00:22:06,510 --> 00:22:08,100
Of course.

163
00:22:08,601 --> 00:22:12,751
But this time, I'll let him know
that it's the emperor's wish.

164
00:22:13,875 --> 00:22:15,925
Osman will still refuse.

165
00:22:15,932 --> 00:22:17,902
I know this, Mari.

166
00:22:18,375 --> 00:22:21,935
But his time, he won't
be facing Lord Rogatus.

167
00:22:23,811 --> 00:22:28,891
It's Michael Kosses with the
support of the Byzantine Emperor.

168
00:22:30,388 --> 00:22:35,288
It's time that Osman realizes this.

169
00:22:52,791 --> 00:22:56,891
Come on, alps!
We need to return before the sun fall!

170
00:23:07,889 --> 00:23:12,389
Bala? Won't you talk to me?

171
00:23:17,679 --> 00:23:21,019
The arrogance you showed to Gökçe
hurt the whole tribe.

172
00:23:22,044 --> 00:23:24,444
Wouldn't you be mad?

173
00:23:27,700 --> 00:23:30,391
If you are showing weakness,
who should I trust?

174
00:23:30,391 --> 00:23:33,521
You are right, Bala.
I made a mistake.

175
00:23:34,229 --> 00:23:35,759
Forgive me.

176
00:24:12,749 --> 00:24:15,059
Can I shoot, Osman Bey?

177
00:24:16,778 --> 00:24:18,728
Here, Kosses.

178
00:24:46,544 --> 00:24:47,834
Bala.

179
00:24:48,818 --> 00:24:51,198
Will you stay resentful?

180
00:25:01,005 --> 00:25:03,625
Can one stay resentful to her sister?

181
00:25:10,197 --> 00:25:11,947
Bala.

182
00:25:42,821 --> 00:25:46,201
You'll be in my hands soon.

183
00:26:08,627 --> 00:26:11,077
Alps! Watch out!

184
00:26:12,047 --> 00:26:14,157
Bala, be careful!

185
00:26:32,600 --> 00:26:37,830
We'll kick Osman out of these
lands!

186
00:26:37,840 --> 00:26:39,830
You vile dog!

187
00:27:36,309 --> 00:27:37,799
My child!

188
00:27:40,303 --> 00:27:41,493
My child!

189
00:27:50,004 --> 00:27:52,374
Bala! Bala!

190
00:27:52,769 --> 00:27:54,959
-Bala!
-We are retreating!

191
00:27:59,082 --> 00:28:01,897
-Bala!
-My child...

192
00:28:04,007 --> 00:28:05,967
Bala!
Bala!

193
00:28:07,717 --> 00:28:08,907
Bala!

194
00:28:09,233 --> 00:28:11,533
Bala!

195
00:28:11,597 --> 00:28:14,154
You are a strong woman.

196
00:28:14,154 --> 00:28:16,404
Hang on!

197
00:28:19,601 --> 00:28:21,651
My child...

198
00:28:26,353 --> 00:28:28,543
My child...

199
00:28:37,137 --> 00:28:38,843
Bala, stay strong!

200
00:28:38,843 --> 00:28:41,853
We are returning to the tribe!
Come on!

201
00:28:42,679 --> 00:28:45,299
Bala! Bala!

202
00:28:48,050 --> 00:28:50,910
Using a Turkish bow takes skill.

203
00:28:51,707 --> 00:28:53,157
After all...

204
00:28:54,282 --> 00:28:58,522
the bow is short,
the arrow is short...

205
00:29:02,563 --> 00:29:04,293
the draw is short.

206
00:29:21,799 --> 00:29:25,169
You seem to carry that skill, Osman Bey.

207
00:29:25,936 --> 00:29:28,446
You didn't come here to watch
archery drill, Kosses.

208
00:29:29,857 --> 00:29:32,777
You know well why I'm here.

209
00:29:35,406 --> 00:29:37,146
Priest Gregor.

210
00:29:37,853 --> 00:29:41,333
Holding someone that the emperor
wants this much...

211
00:29:42,533 --> 00:29:44,573
is a brave act.

212
00:29:48,130 --> 00:29:51,510
But when is it seen that bravery
stops destruction?

213
00:29:55,457 --> 00:29:57,617
If you insist...

214
00:29:59,855 --> 00:30:04,235
the emperor will be so mad.
There will be heavy retaliations.

215
00:30:04,996 --> 00:30:07,306
The news spread as fast as my arrows.

216
00:30:07,857 --> 00:30:10,027
I didn't expect you this soon.

217
00:30:10,473 --> 00:30:13,263
Bhytinia is a small place.

218
00:30:13,861 --> 00:30:15,971
So, what's your offer, Kosses?

219
00:30:17,491 --> 00:30:21,111
Should we give you the priest and
relieve from all burden?

220
00:30:21,713 --> 00:30:25,513
Yes, that's exactly what I'm offering,
Osman Bey.

221
00:30:27,892 --> 00:30:32,182
It's in your hands to end it before
it's getting any worse.

222
00:30:36,821 --> 00:30:40,081
If you continue like this, I'm afraid
the emperor...

223
00:30:40,527 --> 00:30:44,117
We've been living with you in these
lands for a long time.

224
00:30:45,498 --> 00:30:49,268
I thought you knew about the Turks.

225
00:30:52,350 --> 00:30:55,560
Priest Gregor took refuge in us.

226
00:30:57,521 --> 00:31:01,211
Not you, even if the emperor
himself comes here...

227
00:31:01,632 --> 00:31:04,132
he can't take someone who took
refuge in us.

228
00:31:08,482 --> 00:31:10,252
Tell this to the emperor.

229
00:31:55,681 --> 00:32:03,633
-Allah is immortal!
-Allah is just!

230
00:32:04,275 --> 00:32:07,206
My bey, who's sword is this?

231
00:32:07,206 --> 00:32:11,196
Who would it be, master?
My son Orhan!

232
00:32:11,906 --> 00:32:14,936
Mashallah!
Allah is immortal!

233
00:32:14,962 --> 00:32:17,572
Allah is just!

234
00:32:29,688 --> 00:32:31,518
Alaca?

235
00:32:36,927 --> 00:32:38,597
Alaca!

236
00:32:46,469 --> 00:32:48,659
Stay calm.

237
00:32:57,855 --> 00:33:00,665
Tell me what happened.
What happened?

238
00:33:20,032 --> 00:33:23,042
Mother Selcan!

239
00:33:33,560 --> 00:33:35,170
Bala!

240
00:33:39,035 --> 00:33:40,535
Bala!

241
00:33:46,963 --> 00:33:49,193
Bala! Bala!

242
00:33:52,118 --> 00:33:53,466
Bala!

243
00:33:53,466 --> 00:33:55,786
Speak! What is this?

244
00:33:55,915 --> 00:33:58,605
What happened?

245
00:33:58,897 --> 00:34:01,422
Who did this?

246
00:34:01,422 --> 00:34:03,442
Tell me!
Who?

247
00:34:03,442 --> 00:34:05,520
She was hit on her belly.

248
00:34:05,520 --> 00:34:07,380
What are you saying?

249
00:34:07,969 --> 00:34:09,329
Osman!

250
00:34:09,697 --> 00:34:12,788
My child...
My baby...

251
00:34:13,516 --> 00:34:15,016
Bala!

252
00:34:17,594 --> 00:34:20,585
Move out of my way!

253
00:34:20,585 --> 00:34:22,896
Osman!

254
00:34:24,482 --> 00:34:26,632
Mother!

255
00:34:27,112 --> 00:34:28,473
Mother!

256
00:34:29,487 --> 00:34:31,889
To the tent! Come on!

257
00:34:31,889 --> 00:34:33,289
Hurry!

258
00:34:33,973 --> 00:34:36,123
Hurry!

259
00:34:38,395 --> 00:34:40,885
Bala, hang on.

260
00:34:41,150 --> 00:34:42,981
Move out!

261
00:34:44,745 --> 00:34:46,665
Come on, mother.

262
00:34:48,214 --> 00:34:49,664
Hang on, Bala.

263
00:34:51,331 --> 00:34:52,851
Hang on!

264
00:35:03,894 --> 00:35:06,584
Mother!
Bala!

265
00:35:07,307 --> 00:35:08,874
Bala!

266
00:35:08,874 --> 00:35:11,464
-Bala!
-Move out!

267
00:35:15,351 --> 00:35:18,921
My pretty daughter...

268
00:35:19,823 --> 00:35:21,413
Stay strong.

269
00:35:22,473 --> 00:35:24,013
Bala.

270
00:35:25,146 --> 00:35:26,826
Mother...

271
00:35:31,137 --> 00:35:35,087
-Speak, mother.
-Her wound is light, son.

272
00:35:35,174 --> 00:35:37,354
-Thank Allah.
-Thank Allah.

273
00:35:37,940 --> 00:35:39,560
Thank Allah.

274
00:35:42,096 --> 00:35:43,676
The baby?

275
00:35:43,812 --> 00:35:45,432
The baby, mother?

276
00:35:53,196 --> 00:35:55,060
-You get out.
-Mother?

277
00:35:55,250 --> 00:35:58,680
-Get out, Osman!
-Don't go!

278
00:36:01,707 --> 00:36:03,827
What if our baby dies...

279
00:36:10,390 --> 00:36:12,400
Don't leave, Osman.

280
00:36:15,115 --> 00:36:18,675
I'm here. Don't worry, I'm here.

281
00:36:18,727 --> 00:36:21,797
Come on, my lion.

282
00:36:21,986 --> 00:36:24,026
Come on.

283
00:36:26,557 --> 00:36:29,547
My pretty girl.
Bring water, come on!

284
00:36:30,386 --> 00:36:33,246
Mother, my child!
My child!

285
00:36:33,246 --> 00:36:34,406
Mother!

286
00:36:40,373 --> 00:36:44,063
You will stay strong, my child.

287
00:36:44,349 --> 00:36:46,159
Mother!

288
00:36:46,159 --> 00:36:49,309
Your child will be alright and
so will you.

289
00:36:53,539 --> 00:36:55,340
Who did this, Malhun?

290
00:36:55,340 --> 00:36:58,690
Catalonians, my bey.
We were returning from Söğüt.

291
00:36:58,690 --> 00:37:00,810
They set an ambush.

292
00:37:01,641 --> 00:37:04,881
We've beaten them, of course.
But...

293
00:37:13,561 --> 00:37:15,831
''We'll banish Osman from
these lands.''

294
00:37:16,935 --> 00:37:19,395
they say.

295
00:37:21,386 --> 00:37:23,366
-Göktuğ.
-My bey.

296
00:37:23,412 --> 00:37:26,892
Gather the alps.
Destroy them!

297
00:37:27,262 --> 00:37:29,212
Create a blood pool!

298
00:37:29,332 --> 00:37:33,592
All the rivers will flow red today!

299
00:37:34,650 --> 00:37:36,450
They will, my bey.

300
00:37:40,857 --> 00:37:42,257
Göktuğ!

301
00:37:43,896 --> 00:37:46,236
Don't let me down!

302
00:37:47,395 --> 00:37:49,445
Bring me his corpse!

303
00:37:51,194 --> 00:37:52,984
As you order, my bey.

304
00:37:53,476 --> 00:37:55,456
Come on, brothers!

305
00:38:17,150 --> 00:38:18,740
My Allah.

306
00:38:20,518 --> 00:38:23,268
Don't give us the loss of a child.

307
00:38:27,450 --> 00:38:30,900
Don't put Bala in despair.

308
00:38:47,095 --> 00:38:48,715
Osman!

309
00:39:32,114 --> 00:39:34,554
Bilecik Castle

310
00:39:45,799 --> 00:39:47,489
Come, Theodor.

311
00:39:50,099 --> 00:39:52,399
Have you found him?

312
00:39:52,677 --> 00:39:55,557
I have, my lord.
I told him what you said.

313
00:39:55,628 --> 00:39:57,874
So, what did he say?

314
00:39:57,874 --> 00:40:02,494
Priest Gregor is my close friend
as much as he is Rogatus'.

315
00:40:04,007 --> 00:40:08,087
He said that he'll do as you want
and learn the truth.

316
00:40:08,635 --> 00:40:11,305
Good. Good.

317
00:40:12,673 --> 00:40:14,363
Good.

318
00:40:29,439 --> 00:40:32,429
Battle without Cerkutay is
too silent.

319
00:40:35,528 --> 00:40:37,488
That mad man.

320
00:40:38,857 --> 00:40:41,307
Where is Cerkutay and Aygül?

321
00:40:43,189 --> 00:40:45,799
My bey must've given them a task.
I don't know.

322
00:40:47,314 --> 00:40:50,472
Catalonians take this road
to their denn.

323
00:40:50,472 --> 00:40:52,092
We won't let them.

324
00:40:52,488 --> 00:40:54,208
We'll strike them.

325
00:40:56,002 --> 00:40:58,032
Be ready.

326
00:41:00,047 --> 00:41:02,077
They might be here any moment.

327
00:41:07,418 --> 00:41:11,488
Let's not let our bey down.
Let's do this as we need to.

328
00:41:13,453 --> 00:41:16,893
We'll kill those dogs, inshallah.

329
00:41:16,903 --> 00:41:18,463
Alright.

330
00:41:24,800 --> 00:41:27,550
They are coming, my bey.
They aren't many.

331
00:41:33,767 --> 00:41:36,637
Come on!
To your positions!

332
00:41:59,944 --> 00:42:02,024
Where are they?

333
00:42:32,441 --> 00:42:34,261
An ambush!

334
00:42:40,140 --> 00:42:42,530
Come on! Come on, Göktuğ!

335
00:42:59,948 --> 00:43:01,028
Allah Allah!

336
00:44:25,270 --> 00:44:27,520
Stand closer, alps!
Stand closer!

337
00:44:48,077 --> 00:44:49,697
Stop!

338
00:45:00,685 --> 00:45:02,895
Isn't Osman Bey here?

339
00:45:03,388 --> 00:45:05,948
I thought he would come personally.

340
00:45:06,217 --> 00:45:07,987
My bey isn't required to kill you.

341
00:45:16,226 --> 00:45:17,886
Wait.

342
00:45:22,354 --> 00:45:23,784
Come on!

343
00:45:28,280 --> 00:45:32,710
This isn't good. Come with Osman Bey
next time.

344
00:45:32,785 --> 00:45:37,865
We will return, Anselmo!
We will return!

345
00:45:56,382 --> 00:45:58,062
Osman!

346
00:46:09,682 --> 00:46:11,222
Bala!

347
00:46:11,365 --> 00:46:12,805
-Bala!
-Thank Allah.

348
00:46:14,976 --> 00:46:16,426
Are you alright?

349
00:46:17,242 --> 00:46:19,212
Our child...

350
00:46:20,665 --> 00:46:23,705
Mother, is my baby alright?

351
00:46:24,553 --> 00:46:26,323
Is my child healthy, mother?

352
00:46:26,762 --> 00:46:29,732
-Mother?
-You are both healthy, thank Allah.

353
00:46:34,230 --> 00:46:35,860
Thank Allah.

354
00:46:39,720 --> 00:46:41,540
Thank Allah.

355
00:46:43,132 --> 00:46:44,602
Mother...

356
00:46:47,494 --> 00:46:49,704
This is a miracle.

357
00:46:51,246 --> 00:46:52,936
Mashallah.

358
00:46:59,513 --> 00:47:01,883
-Bala.
-Mother.

359
00:47:07,183 --> 00:47:08,916
Thank Allah, son.

360
00:47:13,519 --> 00:47:15,499
Thank Allah.

361
00:47:30,396 --> 00:47:32,196
Thank Allah.

362
00:47:35,894 --> 00:47:38,034
I was so afraid, Osman.

363
00:47:38,180 --> 00:47:40,760
I was so afraid to lose him.

364
00:47:42,516 --> 00:47:44,046
Bala.

365
00:47:45,232 --> 00:47:47,052
I was in many battles...

366
00:47:49,037 --> 00:47:51,157
I've overcome many calamities...

367
00:47:52,517 --> 00:47:54,187
but today...

368
00:47:57,474 --> 00:47:59,804
I was never as afraid as
I was today.

369
00:48:00,666 --> 00:48:03,146
I was so afraid to lose you.

370
00:48:03,786 --> 00:48:06,236
That something could happen to you...

371
00:48:07,735 --> 00:48:11,655
I was so afraid that something could
happen to our baby.

372
00:48:14,499 --> 00:48:16,309
Thank Allah.

373
00:48:18,696 --> 00:48:20,576
Thank Allah.

374
00:48:21,519 --> 00:48:23,209
Thank Allah

375
00:48:33,185 --> 00:48:35,075
I brought soup, my bey.

376
00:48:36,440 --> 00:48:38,010
Malhun.

377
00:48:38,212 --> 00:48:40,272
Come, come.

378
00:49:03,426 --> 00:49:05,956
Slowly, slowly.

379
00:49:07,689 --> 00:49:08,789
Slowly.

380
00:49:09,412 --> 00:49:11,562
With the name of Allah.

381
00:49:11,562 --> 00:49:12,842
May it heal you.

382
00:49:51,775 --> 00:49:53,834
Harmankaya Castle

383
00:49:53,834 --> 00:49:57,864
Tell me, Bahadır.
How is our priest?

384
00:49:59,010 --> 00:50:01,340
They have been protecting him
better than ever.

385
00:50:01,954 --> 00:50:04,904
They even examine the food.

386
00:50:06,270 --> 00:50:08,380
We already know that.

387
00:50:10,267 --> 00:50:14,617
However, they can't stop someone brave
like you...

388
00:50:16,686 --> 00:50:19,986
with these precautions.

389
00:50:23,507 --> 00:50:27,507
You will kill that Priest...

390
00:50:29,354 --> 00:50:31,284
Bahadır.

391
00:50:41,254 --> 00:50:44,854
I do all these just to
live, Kosses.

392
00:50:47,205 --> 00:50:50,995
If I die at the end
of it, what's the point?

393
00:50:52,372 --> 00:50:55,232
Of course.

394
00:51:10,271 --> 00:51:12,841
Thanks for the offer...

395
00:51:13,449 --> 00:51:14,949
Sir Kosses.

396
00:51:31,570 --> 00:51:35,880
You can't get out of here alive, Bahadır.

397
00:51:37,494 --> 00:51:41,114
However, if you try to
kill Priest Gregor...

398
00:51:41,665 --> 00:51:44,905
you may have a chance to live.

399
00:51:49,281 --> 00:51:53,281
If you change your mind when
you get out of here...

400
00:51:53,879 --> 00:51:58,209
just know that you are not protected as
much as Priest Gregor.

401
00:52:10,342 --> 00:52:12,922
I will do everything I can.

402
00:52:14,605 --> 00:52:17,125
That's what I thought.

403
00:52:17,980 --> 00:52:20,380
You can leave.

404
00:52:29,105 --> 00:52:31,815
Do you think he will succeed?

405
00:52:34,162 --> 00:52:37,322
- If you want, the Emperor can help...
- No!

406
00:52:37,900 --> 00:52:40,690
No!

407
00:52:42,522 --> 00:52:45,502
The Emperor already knows everything.

408
00:52:46,078 --> 00:52:50,268
I already feel humiliated because I can
not take Priest back.

409
00:52:51,252 --> 00:52:53,962
I can't let that happen again.

410
00:52:54,711 --> 00:52:57,581
Bahadır will kill the Priest.

411
00:52:58,115 --> 00:53:01,905
I will serve his dead body to the Emperor.

412
00:53:02,514 --> 00:53:04,304
That's it.

413
00:53:34,436 --> 00:53:36,486
Can I come in, my Bey?

414
00:53:37,515 --> 00:53:39,845
Come in.

415
00:54:05,520 --> 00:54:08,270
I can't look at your face, my Bey.

416
00:54:18,119 --> 00:54:20,539
I don't deserve to be your Alp.

417
00:54:23,353 --> 00:54:25,733
You can punish me, my Bey.

418
00:54:43,125 --> 00:54:45,735
I deserve what you will do to me.

419
00:54:51,474 --> 00:54:54,064
You couldn't punish those dogs who
tried to kill...

420
00:54:57,185 --> 00:55:00,375
my Hatun...

421
00:55:02,561 --> 00:55:06,771
and other Hatuns in the tent.

422
00:55:16,875 --> 00:55:19,285
I told you to kill them!

423
00:55:20,494 --> 00:55:22,454
You couldn't!

424
00:55:23,476 --> 00:55:26,106
You couldn't kill them!

425
00:55:26,954 --> 00:55:30,654
You had so many horses but you couldn't
ride onto them!

426
00:55:38,048 --> 00:55:40,978
You didn't take revenge of my Hatun.

427
00:55:41,636 --> 00:55:43,696
You disappointed me.

428
00:55:47,360 --> 00:55:51,360
Get out of here!

429
00:56:28,252 --> 00:56:31,642
The castle is well protected, my Bey.

430
00:56:32,274 --> 00:56:35,964
Nikola is a coward. Of course he
is cautious.

431
00:56:37,172 --> 00:56:38,372
Yes he is.

432
00:56:39,685 --> 00:56:42,265
However, he will get out of there.

433
00:56:42,606 --> 00:56:45,036
Then we will catch him.

434
00:56:47,554 --> 00:56:50,954
I want to know his every step.

435
00:56:51,390 --> 00:56:54,240
Your command, my Bey.
He is being watched in the castle.

436
00:56:54,504 --> 00:56:58,144
Thank you.

437
00:56:59,637 --> 00:57:04,447
I won't feel comfortable ever...

438
00:57:04,803 --> 00:57:07,153
before I punish those dogs.

439
00:57:07,388 --> 00:57:11,968
First Nikola, then Rogatus...

440
00:57:11,978 --> 00:57:15,978
and Kosses! They will pay for
what they have done.

441
00:57:17,923 --> 00:57:20,913
And Catalans.

442
00:57:22,298 --> 00:57:24,788
I have news.

443
00:57:24,992 --> 00:57:28,992
Göktuğ, the Alp of Osman Bey, attacked
Catalans.

444
00:57:32,125 --> 00:57:36,125
- Did they succeed?
- No, my Bey.

445
00:57:38,634 --> 00:57:43,624
If Osman Bey didn't succeed in this, we
should beat Catalans.

446
00:57:45,729 --> 00:57:48,249
Follow these ignobles.

447
00:57:48,599 --> 00:57:51,269
We will take revenge on them too.

448
00:57:52,123 --> 00:57:54,883
Your command, my Bey.

449
00:58:23,630 --> 00:58:25,080
My Bala.

450
00:58:26,104 --> 00:58:28,904
Drink this. May it be good for you.

451
00:58:30,120 --> 00:58:34,260
Bismillâhirrahmânirrahîm. (in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

452
00:58:37,052 --> 00:58:42,092
Mashallah.

453
00:58:42,563 --> 00:58:44,583
Can I come in?

454
00:58:46,859 --> 00:58:50,859
Come in, my Sheikh.
Come in.

455
00:59:01,307 --> 00:59:03,867
My daughter.

456
00:59:05,429 --> 00:59:08,869
Please feel comfortable.

457
00:59:10,125 --> 00:59:14,125
My Sheikh, welcome.

458
00:59:20,753 --> 00:59:24,593
I was afraid, my Sheikh.

459
00:59:27,771 --> 00:59:31,771
Thank Allah...

460
00:59:47,842 --> 00:59:51,842
Bismillâhirrahmânirrahîm. (in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

461
00:59:56,128 --> 01:00:00,368
Your mother wrapped you with this.

462
01:00:03,639 --> 01:00:06,959
You will wrap your child with this.

463
01:00:13,592 --> 01:00:21,222
Thank Allah that you and my
grandchild is healthy.

464
01:00:24,347 --> 01:00:30,037
Bad things happen.

465
01:00:33,541 --> 01:00:38,991
Your sadness will make you forgiven in the
afterlife.

466
01:00:40,518 --> 01:00:42,438
Amin

467
01:00:42,773 --> 01:00:45,883
Amin, my Sheikh.

468
01:00:47,531 --> 01:00:56,221
While one of you is under the sun, another
can't sit under the cloud.

469
01:01:01,781 --> 01:01:06,331
When Hadrat Hatice...

470
01:01:06,827 --> 01:01:12,347
felt love towards Hadrat Muhammad...

471
01:01:13,686 --> 01:01:20,546
she did everything.

472
01:01:22,938 --> 01:01:26,938
When a woman loved a man...

473
01:01:27,689 --> 01:01:30,459
it was seen as a sin.

474
01:01:31,509 --> 01:01:37,119
Our Hadrat Hatice's love
for our Prophet...

475
01:01:37,323 --> 01:01:42,053
was so big that she didn't care...

476
01:01:42,551 --> 01:01:48,901
about what people said and she wanted
to marry.

477
01:01:51,161 --> 01:01:57,301
Our Prophet felt the same and...

478
01:01:57,658 --> 01:02:03,498
he and our mother Hadrat Hatice...

479
01:02:05,423 --> 01:02:10,133
married.

480
01:02:11,536 --> 01:02:17,966
While everyone was against Muhammad
Mustafa, whose name is a beauty...

481
01:02:18,793 --> 01:02:21,733
"may the blessings of Allah be upon him!"

482
01:02:22,385 --> 01:02:26,905
our mother Hadrat Hatice...

483
01:02:27,313 --> 01:02:30,763
always protected and...

484
01:02:31,171 --> 01:02:35,491
sided with our Prophet.

485
01:02:37,142 --> 01:02:43,362
Our mother Hatice was so in love with our
Prophet that...

486
01:02:43,543 --> 01:02:47,543
while our Prophet made his way to tell
about Islan to other people...

487
01:02:48,268 --> 01:02:52,268
our mother Hatice waited under the sun...

488
01:02:52,878 --> 01:02:57,548
as she didn't want to wait under the clouds...

489
01:02:58,174 --> 01:03:04,244
while he was under the sun.

490
01:03:04,896 --> 01:03:09,146
She waited under the sun.

491
01:03:11,056 --> 01:03:14,506
Thanks to her.

492
01:03:14,888 --> 01:03:18,368
Thanks to her.

493
01:03:18,494 --> 01:03:24,144
The love between
Hadrat Hatice and Our Prophet...

494
01:03:24,160 --> 01:03:26,170
affected you the same.

495
01:03:26,619 --> 01:03:30,619
May Allah make it forever.

496
01:03:30,747 --> 01:03:34,747
- Amin.
- Amin, my Sheikh.

497
01:03:55,153 --> 01:03:56,933
Brother.

498
01:04:15,049 --> 01:04:17,239
My brother.

499
01:04:17,550 --> 01:04:20,140
I wish he was mad at me.

500
01:04:20,581 --> 01:04:23,701
I wish he hit me.

501
01:04:24,585 --> 01:04:27,355
So that I would feel myself.

502
01:04:31,575 --> 01:04:34,565
I couldn't be worthy of him.

503
01:04:37,081 --> 01:04:38,531
Göktuğ.

504
01:04:39,345 --> 01:04:42,395
You still don't listen to our Bey.

505
01:04:44,916 --> 01:04:48,316
If he didn't hit you, that's because he
wanted you to be strong.

506
01:04:53,907 --> 01:04:58,867
It's time to be strong and be worthy
of Osman Bey.

507
01:04:59,584 --> 01:05:01,424
Come on.

508
01:05:43,022 --> 01:05:45,122
Welcome, Priest.

509
01:05:47,206 --> 01:05:50,246
Just sit and let's talk.

510
01:05:50,448 --> 01:05:54,448
You don't need to be kind. You know
I'm not here willingly.

511
01:05:54,844 --> 01:05:57,894
You made me come back here.

512
01:05:59,714 --> 01:06:01,944
Not me.

513
01:06:03,916 --> 01:06:05,706
This.

514
01:06:11,095 --> 01:06:13,545
We both know that...

515
01:06:14,465 --> 01:06:17,775
you're here for this.

516
01:06:21,472 --> 01:06:24,912
As it's bringing you here, it's something
important...

517
01:06:25,804 --> 01:06:29,024
tell me, what's that?

518
01:06:29,960 --> 01:06:32,130
It's a heirloom.

519
01:06:32,900 --> 01:06:36,900
It belongs to my grandfather.
We have it for years.

520
01:06:36,968 --> 01:06:41,588
I want to give it to next
generations if you let me.

521
01:06:44,736 --> 01:06:48,446
You hide it from your friend Rogatus...

522
01:06:51,298 --> 01:06:53,808
it must be really valuable.

523
01:06:53,992 --> 01:06:56,272
It is!

524
01:06:59,679 --> 01:07:00,979
It is.

525
01:07:02,185 --> 01:07:05,685
How do you know that?
Rogatus --

526
01:07:09,352 --> 01:07:12,192
He was here.

527
01:07:15,228 --> 01:07:18,638
When I told him what brought you
here is an heirloom...

528
01:07:19,794 --> 01:07:21,944
he was surprised.

529
01:07:22,206 --> 01:07:24,356
He was curious.

530
01:07:30,965 --> 01:07:33,205
I understand that...

531
01:07:33,476 --> 01:07:38,176
he doesn't know about that heirloom.

532
01:07:40,210 --> 01:07:43,400
He doesn't.

533
01:07:43,549 --> 01:07:46,849
It's not that I don't trust him.

534
01:07:47,028 --> 01:07:51,028
It's an heirloom. It's normal that
he doesn't know.

535
01:07:51,433 --> 01:07:53,873
He knows now.

536
01:07:55,286 --> 01:07:58,526
Do you still trust Rogatus?

537
01:08:00,649 --> 01:08:04,089
I always trust him, Osman Bey.

538
01:08:07,679 --> 01:08:11,049
This trust will harm you, Priest.

539
01:08:11,934 --> 01:08:13,924
Be careful.

540
01:08:15,951 --> 01:08:19,201
Rogatus only wants to be stronger.

541
01:08:19,285 --> 01:08:21,805
You call him your friend...

542
01:08:22,523 --> 01:08:25,363
however, he uses you.

543
01:08:34,763 --> 01:08:38,023
You think this heirloom
doesn't interest him...

544
01:08:40,008 --> 01:08:42,778
I've seen his face.

545
01:08:46,828 --> 01:08:50,337
If he knows that this heirloom...

546
01:08:50,675 --> 01:08:53,745
will make him stronger...

547
01:08:55,283 --> 01:08:58,033
then he will go after it.

548
01:08:58,973 --> 01:09:02,973
- You're wrong, Osman Bey.
- Then you will meet face to face.

549
01:09:06,359 --> 01:09:09,499
However, this heirloom won't be with you.

550
01:09:10,024 --> 01:09:14,795
Let's see whether he will
choose you or this.

551
01:09:17,814 --> 01:09:20,955
Why are we doing this?

552
01:09:21,809 --> 01:09:25,029
I want to know your real intention.

553
01:09:26,719 --> 01:09:30,038
What do you want from me, Osman Bey?

554
01:09:31,901 --> 01:09:35,201
I want you to see what I saw, Priest.

555
01:09:36,691 --> 01:09:40,331
In Bithynia, you and your heirloom...

556
01:09:40,413 --> 01:09:45,834
isn't safe.

557
01:09:46,968 --> 01:09:50,207
What if you're wrong?

558
01:09:50,540 --> 01:09:53,390
What if Rogatus is loyal?

559
01:09:53,590 --> 01:09:56,610
What if he treats me well?

560
01:09:57,763 --> 01:10:00,733
Then I will set you free.

561
01:10:05,091 --> 01:10:08,381
I will give your heirloom to you.

562
01:10:12,503 --> 01:10:14,183
Okay.

563
01:10:21,359 --> 01:10:23,279
I accept.

564
01:10:23,922 --> 01:10:27,922
How do we meet Rogatus?

565
01:10:29,837 --> 01:10:32,817
We shouldn't attract Rogatus' attention.

566
01:10:33,212 --> 01:10:37,402
Osman Bey, send me back to church.

567
01:10:39,971 --> 01:10:42,741
Rogatus will contact me.

568
01:10:47,317 --> 01:10:50,027
What are you thinking, Priest?

569
01:10:50,829 --> 01:10:53,019
Osman Bey...

570
01:10:59,407 --> 01:11:03,407
I'm grateful that you're here.

571
01:11:03,904 --> 01:11:07,734
Bithynia is small. The news spread.

572
01:11:08,125 --> 01:11:10,365
You must have heard that...

573
01:11:10,399 --> 01:11:13,669
Bey of Kayı, Osman has the Priest Gregor.

574
01:11:14,122 --> 01:11:15,992
We heard that bad news.

575
01:11:16,219 --> 01:11:19,349
You couldn't protect a Priest.

576
01:11:23,869 --> 01:11:27,869
Osman aims to disrupt the...

577
01:11:28,267 --> 01:11:31,947
unity of Christians.

578
01:11:32,761 --> 01:11:38,691
As much as I know, Priest Gregor was
doing the same, Rogatus.

579
01:11:41,867 --> 01:11:45,867
He was disrupting the unity of Christians
by going against the Emperor.

580
01:11:47,233 --> 01:11:50,906
I just wanted to save my friend's life...

581
01:11:50,906 --> 01:11:54,226
it's not about Osman, right Kosses?

582
01:11:55,893 --> 01:11:59,283
If Osman continues to keeping Gregor...

583
01:11:59,589 --> 01:12:03,189
he can have a say on
the Christian community.

584
01:12:03,249 --> 01:12:07,249
That's why we should leave
the conflict among us and...

585
01:12:07,392 --> 01:12:09,262
be together.

586
01:12:09,556 --> 01:12:14,556
It's the only way we can make
Osman give Gregor back to us.

587
01:12:15,954 --> 01:12:19,334
Do you want to tell us how, Rogatus?

588
01:12:21,938 --> 01:12:24,598
Well, my dear friend...

589
01:12:25,345 --> 01:12:29,345
we will stop everything they will
make benefit from.

590
01:12:32,557 --> 01:12:34,007
For example...

591
01:12:34,270 --> 01:12:36,630
the Turkmen employees
working in their mines...

592
01:12:36,817 --> 01:12:40,817
my employees were teaching them
the key points of this job but...

593
01:12:41,610 --> 01:12:46,560
I dismissed those vain people
because they didn't deserve...

594
01:12:46,560 --> 01:12:50,114
to know this information.

595
01:12:53,016 --> 01:12:57,936
My dear friend, Manuel, the
governor of İznik...

596
01:13:00,586 --> 01:13:03,866
he broke the agreements with tradesmen
in Söğüt.

597
01:13:04,019 --> 01:13:05,949
Right?

598
01:13:06,135 --> 01:13:10,165
I assure you that Osman, the
Bey of Kayı...

599
01:13:10,191 --> 01:13:13,411
is dreaming...

600
01:13:13,644 --> 01:13:16,194
to be Süleyman Shah, son of the devil.

601
01:13:16,229 --> 01:13:21,239
That's why my dear friend, Manuel, the
governor of İznik...

602
01:13:22,118 --> 01:13:25,408
won't buy any Kayı rug.

603
01:13:25,560 --> 01:13:29,790
We are breaking the agreement.
We won't buy any Kayı rug.

604
01:13:30,913 --> 01:13:34,493
I want you to do the same thing.

605
01:13:36,114 --> 01:13:37,894
Trade.

606
01:13:40,831 --> 01:13:43,061
Trade...

607
01:13:46,545 --> 01:13:49,495
is like a river...

608
01:13:50,546 --> 01:13:53,196
when the river gets dry...

609
01:13:58,468 --> 01:14:01,548
people around it...

610
01:14:01,733 --> 01:14:04,453
start fighting.

611
01:14:10,705 --> 01:14:12,395
Rogatus...

612
01:14:13,766 --> 01:14:16,636
it's a well-thought idea.

613
01:14:26,373 --> 01:14:29,063
I agree with Nikola.

614
01:14:31,906 --> 01:14:34,356
Let's be together.

615
01:15:02,578 --> 01:15:06,578
-You know the bey's order, Saltuk.
-I do, brother.

616
01:15:06,578 --> 01:15:09,418
We'll leave them so that Gregor
can talk to the old man.

617
01:15:10,308 --> 01:15:15,278
-But I don't understand why.
-Beys have secrets.

618
01:15:16,031 --> 01:15:18,641
Come on.

619
01:15:42,549 --> 01:15:46,979
You surprised me.
Why did you--

620
01:15:46,979 --> 01:15:52,169
-We'll run away from the tribe. Help us.
-How can I help?

621
01:15:52,169 --> 01:15:57,219
It's impossible. Osman Bey must've
taken every measure.

622
01:15:57,219 --> 01:16:02,589
I planned everything. Just be at the
entrance of the tribe at the dawn.

623
01:16:02,589 --> 01:16:07,779
You'll wait for us with two horses.
We'll go to the forest.

624
01:16:09,259 --> 01:16:14,729
-Tell Rogatus to meet us there.
-It'll be difficult but alright.

625
01:16:15,631 --> 01:16:17,821
I'll do it.

626
01:16:23,507 --> 01:16:27,507
Well done, ladies.

627
01:16:27,507 --> 01:16:31,507
-Thank Allah you've done it.
-Thank you, Mother Selcan.

628
01:17:01,796 --> 01:17:05,796
Welcome, it's just time.
The carpets are ready.

629
01:17:05,796 --> 01:17:10,796
They are waiting to be loaded.
But the carts?

630
01:17:10,796 --> 01:17:15,576
Carts aren't coming. The agreement
is canceled. We aren't buying.

631
01:17:15,576 --> 01:17:19,136
Wait there.
What does that mean?

632
01:17:19,136 --> 01:17:23,196
I don't know. I'm tasked to inform.

633
01:17:35,783 --> 01:17:39,423
What's this.
What is he saying, son?

634
01:17:39,423 --> 01:17:43,783
They've broken the agreement.
They aren't buying.

635
01:17:44,564 --> 01:17:49,534
-What will we do now?
-I don't know, mother. I don't know.

636
01:17:51,377 --> 01:17:55,527
We need to inform Osman Bey.
If you allow me.

637
01:18:40,738 --> 01:18:46,478
Cornelia, I didn't expect to have
so much fun here.

638
01:18:46,478 --> 01:18:52,228
Your brother will be mad to hear
that we came here.

639
01:18:52,228 --> 01:18:57,528
I can't help it. This tribe takes
you into itself.

640
01:18:58,270 --> 01:19:02,670
What does changing minds at the
delivery date means?

641
01:19:03,325 --> 01:19:07,145
There is something behind this.

642
01:19:07,892 --> 01:19:11,892
What'll happen to all the carpets?

643
01:19:12,325 --> 01:19:17,405
Is İznik the only place to sell our
carpets to?

644
01:19:17,405 --> 01:19:22,165
Don't worry, ladies. Osman Bey
will find a way.

645
01:19:22,165 --> 01:19:26,735
-Inshallah.
-Get to your work.

646
01:19:52,535 --> 01:19:56,535
-Welcome, Mari.
-Welcome, my child.

647
01:19:56,694 --> 01:19:59,624
Thank you.

648
01:20:00,517 --> 01:20:04,517
This is my helper, Cornelia.
I wanted to introduce her to you.

649
01:20:04,517 --> 01:20:08,517
She was curious about the
process.

650
01:20:09,695 --> 01:20:13,695
Welcome, my child.

651
01:20:16,323 --> 01:20:20,323
Carpets. Where are they going to?

652
01:20:21,003 --> 01:20:25,003
It was supposed to be İznik but
we just received a messenger.

653
01:20:25,093 --> 01:20:29,153
-They changed their mind.
-Why?

654
01:20:29,988 --> 01:20:33,988
We don't know. The messenger
didn't say anything.

655
01:20:33,988 --> 01:20:36,798
We'll find out when Osman Bey returns.

656
01:20:36,989 --> 01:20:39,909
I'm sorry.

657
01:20:39,909 --> 01:20:43,719
I came here to watch
the weaving of the carpets.

658
01:20:43,777 --> 01:20:47,777
Come on, then.
Let's show you.

659
01:20:47,777 --> 01:20:50,797
See how your carpets
are made.

660
01:20:54,548 --> 01:20:56,898
Come.

661
01:21:18,544 --> 01:21:22,284
-Good day.
-Welcome, my bey.

662
01:21:22,284 --> 01:21:24,654
Thank you. Thank you.

663
01:21:27,162 --> 01:21:30,052
-Good day.
-Welcome, my bey.

664
01:21:30,052 --> 01:21:32,342
Thank you.
Thank you.

665
01:21:32,496 --> 01:21:35,266
Have a good working day.

666
01:21:35,536 --> 01:21:39,536
-Welcome, my bey.
-Welcome.

667
01:21:42,387 --> 01:21:46,387
-How is your trade?
-Thank God it's good, my bad.

668
01:21:46,550 --> 01:21:50,550
-Come.
-May Allah bless you.

669
01:21:50,963 --> 01:21:54,963
-Good day.
-Thank you, my bey. Welcome.

670
01:21:56,710 --> 01:22:01,510
Thank you.
Are you making enough?

671
01:22:01,510 --> 01:22:05,240
Yes, my bey. Thank God.

672
01:22:05,240 --> 01:22:10,950
-How is your trade.
-We work day and night for the orders.

673
01:22:11,414 --> 01:22:15,414
It seems like we'll be very happy
after the sales.

674
01:22:15,414 --> 01:22:19,414
-Inshallah, inshallah. May it prosper.
-Thank you, my bey.

675
01:22:24,013 --> 01:22:27,613
-Göktuğ.
-My bey.

676
01:22:27,613 --> 01:22:32,703
As you said, they are whispering.
They must be after something.

677
01:22:36,356 --> 01:22:40,926
-Now, take Gregor back to the tribe.
-As you order, my bey.

678
01:22:59,424 --> 01:23:04,464
-What is this, Baran?
-My bey, they are from Dudullu Tribe.

679
01:23:04,917 --> 01:23:08,917
Sheik Edebali sent them...

680
01:23:08,917 --> 01:23:12,917
to work in Rogatus' mines.

681
01:23:14,209 --> 01:23:17,089
We'll find out now.

682
01:23:20,672 --> 01:23:24,672
-Salam Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam.

683
01:23:24,979 --> 01:23:28,289
Now, tell me.
what is this?

684
01:23:28,289 --> 01:23:33,379
We were working in the silver mines
of the lord of Bilecik.

685
01:23:33,753 --> 01:23:37,753
He said ''Such an important job...

686
01:23:37,753 --> 01:23:41,753
can't be done by such worthless people''
and he kicked us out.

687
01:23:45,536 --> 01:23:49,536
You know the reason.

688
01:23:50,007 --> 01:23:54,007
-Osman Bey.
-Brother.

689
01:23:54,635 --> 01:23:57,905
It's not good, Osman Bey.

690
01:24:01,523 --> 01:24:06,703
-What is it, brother?
-The carpet deal we made with İznik...

691
01:24:07,637 --> 01:24:13,247
the deals we made with the merchants in
Söğüt, they are all canceled.

692
01:24:28,842 --> 01:24:32,552
They are kicking the workers out.

693
01:24:32,809 --> 01:24:36,169
They are canceling the deals.

694
01:24:36,188 --> 01:24:39,808
Their intentions are obvious, brother.

695
01:24:40,051 --> 01:24:45,711
They can't draw their swords but
they try to stop our trade.

696
01:24:48,923 --> 01:24:52,683
It's getting harder, Osman Bey.

697
01:24:52,683 --> 01:24:56,923
We don't like easy, brother.

698
01:24:56,923 --> 01:25:00,923
They try to subjugate us by
doing this.

699
01:25:00,923 --> 01:25:04,923
They think that we'll bow down.

700
01:25:04,923 --> 01:25:08,923
But we bow down before nothing
but Allah.

701
01:25:09,488 --> 01:25:13,488
Now, inform the tribe.

702
01:25:13,488 --> 01:25:17,488
-I want the beys in my tribe.
-Alright, my bey.

703
01:25:19,371 --> 01:25:22,221
Come on.

704
01:25:32,408 --> 01:25:36,678
-Farewell, Bala Hatun.
-Until next time, Mari.

705
01:25:46,996 --> 01:25:52,026
The carpets seem important to them.
They are very sad.

706
01:25:52,026 --> 01:25:56,646
Yes, we'll take them out of
this despair, Cornelia.

707
01:25:57,043 --> 01:26:01,043
Thanks to us, they'll sell
their carpets.

708
01:26:01,043 --> 01:26:05,393
-Will your brother accept this?
-He has to.

709
01:26:05,486 --> 01:26:11,136
If we buy the carpets, they'll believe
in our sincerity.

710
01:26:12,128 --> 01:26:16,128
I don't want to miss the fun, Cornelia.

711
01:26:16,306 --> 01:26:20,306
We'll have much more fun in this tribe.

712
01:27:00,399 --> 01:27:05,049
Turgut Bey, you are freed.

713
01:27:05,628 --> 01:27:09,628
I am, thank Allah.

714
01:27:09,628 --> 01:27:13,628
And we'll punish the ones who
chained me.

715
01:27:16,353 --> 01:27:20,353
I hope you won't fail again.

716
01:27:27,457 --> 01:27:31,457
Why did you help me?

717
01:27:31,947 --> 01:27:35,947
I owed you, Turgut Bey.

718
01:27:37,076 --> 01:27:41,576
Did you forget? You saved me from that
snake.

719
01:27:42,379 --> 01:27:47,179
And by helping you, I honored my debt.

720
01:28:00,287 --> 01:28:03,807
Be careful, Turgut Bey.

721
01:28:04,118 --> 01:28:08,448
I don't have a reason to save you now.

722
01:28:51,711 --> 01:28:53,741
Come on.

723
01:29:00,151 --> 01:29:03,301
Come, my child.

724
01:29:15,183 --> 01:29:18,933
Do you really think she'll buy
the carpets?

725
01:29:19,401 --> 01:29:23,401
I don't know but...

726
01:29:24,006 --> 01:29:27,826
there is something off with
that woman.

727
01:29:29,186 --> 01:29:33,626
I don't feel like she is sincere
with her words.

728
01:29:34,582 --> 01:29:39,642
-It's like she's planning something.
-Time will show.

729
01:29:41,817 --> 01:29:46,537
But if they buy the carpets, they'll
save us from trouble.

730
01:29:49,144 --> 01:29:54,454
Look at these lords. We are happy
that Mari might buy the carpets now.

731
01:29:55,448 --> 01:29:58,928
What will we do now.

732
01:29:58,928 --> 01:30:04,818
Osman Bey will find a way. That's why
he's gathering the beys.

733
01:30:06,051 --> 01:30:10,051
Malhun Hatun is right.

734
01:30:10,221 --> 01:30:14,541
Osman Bey against the whole lords.

735
01:30:14,619 --> 01:30:19,539
He'll unite with his beys
and find a way.

736
01:30:19,556 --> 01:30:23,556
Inshallah. Inshallah.

737
01:30:36,524 --> 01:30:41,134
What should be done to the enemy
who isn't keeping his word, Bala?

738
01:30:43,062 --> 01:30:48,732
One who doesn't keep his word should
be punished regardless of the friendship.

739
01:30:51,647 --> 01:30:55,397
So will we.

740
01:30:55,899 --> 01:31:00,419
Trade isn't only flowing from the east
to the west.

741
01:31:00,419 --> 01:31:06,149
Their caravans move around Turkmen tribes.

742
01:31:10,231 --> 01:31:14,651
We'll find out when will
they pass from where...

743
01:31:14,651 --> 01:31:18,651
so that we can punish them.

744
01:31:21,477 --> 01:31:23,987
My bey.

745
01:31:25,057 --> 01:31:30,657
They are taking their sea caravans from
the narrow strait behind my tribe.

746
01:31:31,689 --> 01:31:36,119
My father Umur Bey never
attacked them.

747
01:31:36,119 --> 01:31:39,639
It's for Osman Bey now.

748
01:31:40,668 --> 01:31:44,668
I heard that they are taking
their spice caravans...

749
01:31:44,668 --> 01:31:48,668
near Yılanlık.

750
01:31:50,325 --> 01:31:54,925
They are protected well,
but not enough.

751
01:31:55,347 --> 01:32:01,737
Tell me then, Turgut Bey.
How many alps can you gather?

752
01:32:04,556 --> 01:32:09,566
All the tribesmen who can wield
a sword is an all of mine.

753
01:32:12,881 --> 01:32:16,881
Just say the word, Osman Bey.

754
01:32:17,386 --> 01:32:22,486
Then, tell your alps.
Osman Bey orders.

755
01:32:23,985 --> 01:32:27,985
We'll know about their routes.

756
01:32:29,294 --> 01:32:33,914
Not a single heathen caravan will
enter Bhytinia.

757
01:32:33,914 --> 01:32:37,124
They won't leave Bhytinia.

758
01:32:38,379 --> 01:32:42,379
-As you order, my bey.
-As you order, my bey.

759
01:32:44,055 --> 01:32:48,965
This war is in between the heathens
and the Muslims.

760
01:32:49,730 --> 01:32:54,310
Their real goal is to
gather under the cross...

761
01:32:54,310 --> 01:32:58,030
and banish us
from these alnds.

762
01:32:59,125 --> 01:33:05,485
We will gather under the light
of the crescent and stand against them.

763
01:33:13,250 --> 01:33:18,910
Their unity is until they
turn their backs against each other.

764
01:33:18,910 --> 01:33:24,310
But our unity has always been
back to back.

765
01:33:29,104 --> 01:33:33,604
-Allah is with us.
-Allah is with us.

766
01:33:34,923 --> 01:33:39,083
Allah is with the believers, my bey.

767
01:33:39,083 --> 01:33:42,663
-May you be victorious.
-Inshallah.

768
01:33:43,611 --> 01:33:47,611
Inshallah.

769
01:33:50,710 --> 01:33:54,070
If you allow me, my bey.

770
01:33:59,971 --> 01:34:03,281
Osman Bey.

771
01:34:05,300 --> 01:34:09,300
Bilecik Castle.

772
01:34:34,385 --> 01:34:38,385
The news is good, Theodor.

773
01:34:38,843 --> 01:34:42,843
Our friend seems to be succesful.

774
01:34:43,205 --> 01:34:46,845
Tomorrow, Gregor will come here.

775
01:34:46,845 --> 01:34:51,605
He'll be with a valuable relic.

776
01:34:51,605 --> 01:34:56,595
You go to the caravan tomorrow.
I'll get the priest.

777
01:35:04,836 --> 01:35:08,836
You took care of my tribe
in my absence.

778
01:35:11,168 --> 01:35:13,398
Thank you.

779
01:35:16,546 --> 01:35:20,996
Did we say all these things for nothing?

780
01:35:22,764 --> 01:35:27,634
It's our duty to tend the wounds
of our brothers.

781
01:35:29,008 --> 01:35:33,008
Then tell me this.

782
01:35:33,770 --> 01:35:37,770
If you knew that Priest Gregor
wouldn't return...

783
01:35:38,060 --> 01:35:41,790
would you still exchange him
with me?

784
01:35:43,181 --> 01:35:47,181
Even the most precious of the heathens...

785
01:35:47,813 --> 01:35:51,533
is not as valuable as you for me.

786
01:35:54,510 --> 01:35:58,510
We wouldn't leave you behind, Turgut Bey.

787
01:36:03,040 --> 01:36:06,230
Thank you.

788
01:36:17,121 --> 01:36:21,121
Turgut Bey's Tribe

789
01:36:25,806 --> 01:36:30,526
It seems that Osman Bey wants
to lead the Turkmens.

790
01:36:31,576 --> 01:36:35,576
Firstly, he should know of us.

791
01:36:36,500 --> 01:36:40,720
Fate will show who will be the head.

792
01:36:41,071 --> 01:36:45,071
Allah decides in the end, right?

793
01:36:52,318 --> 01:36:56,858
We'll do what Osman Bey couldn't.

794
01:36:57,622 --> 01:37:01,622
Tell me what you heard.

795
01:37:01,829 --> 01:37:06,069
My bey, these catolonians
live for gold.

796
01:37:06,069 --> 01:37:10,229
They don't have a home.
They camp in the woods.

797
01:37:10,229 --> 01:37:15,419
Sometimes, they raid caravans.
They worship gold.

798
01:37:16,431 --> 01:37:20,431
So, they raid caravans?

799
01:37:20,639 --> 01:37:25,759
Prepare your alps, Kutan. We'll bury
Anselmo with the gold he raided.

800
01:38:12,034 --> 01:38:16,304
My bey, I heard what happened.

801
01:38:18,517 --> 01:38:24,357
The lords know that they can't beat us.
Now, they are targeting our trade.

802
01:38:27,941 --> 01:38:31,561
Our people will have hard times.

803
01:38:32,038 --> 01:38:36,578
Don't worry, my bey.
Don't think about that.

804
01:38:37,682 --> 01:38:42,482
We'll support the people until
you take care of things.

805
01:38:42,906 --> 01:38:47,206
We'll find a way.

806
01:38:52,015 --> 01:38:56,835
Thank you, Malhun. You always
ease my burden.

807
01:38:58,556 --> 01:39:02,166
You are giving me strenght.

808
01:39:19,151 --> 01:39:22,561
Saltuk!

809
01:39:25,645 --> 01:39:28,425
The priest escaped the church, my bey.

810
01:40:16,649 --> 01:40:19,969
You are coming to your death
with your own feet, Gregor!

811
01:40:20,054 --> 01:40:22,294
You are making my job easier!

812
01:40:23,585 --> 01:40:26,825
- Welcome, Gregor.
- Thank God we reunited.

813
01:40:27,492 --> 01:40:29,432
- We shall leave.
- We shall leave.

814
01:41:12,278 --> 01:41:13,908
What are they doing here?

815
01:41:19,577 --> 01:41:21,007
Let's go.

816
01:41:37,380 --> 01:41:39,600
Do you think they will manage, sir?

817
01:41:41,449 --> 01:41:44,459
I wouldn't be here if I didn't believe
that he'd come.

818
01:41:56,974 --> 01:41:58,894
Gregor, here.

819
01:42:04,248 --> 01:42:05,558
Wait.

820
01:42:06,231 --> 01:42:08,321
We must be sure it's not a trap.

821
01:42:53,435 --> 01:42:54,675
Gregor!

822
01:43:04,931 --> 01:43:07,121
My dear friend Gregor.

823
01:43:08,537 --> 01:43:11,827
I am very, very happy to see you again.

824
01:43:11,827 --> 01:43:14,027
I am too, Lord Rogatus.

825
01:43:19,627 --> 01:43:21,796
The thing that makes you come back...
That relic...

826
01:43:21,796 --> 01:43:23,176
What?

827
01:43:29,185 --> 01:43:30,765
Why did you come back?

828
01:43:34,530 --> 01:43:38,190
What is the precious thing you
forgot in Osman's hand?

829
01:43:42,821 --> 01:43:46,181
Osman must have tricked you.

830
01:43:50,932 --> 01:43:54,252
This was just a little scar.

831
01:43:57,562 --> 01:44:01,072
What is that precious thing that
you hide under your skin?

832
01:44:03,803 --> 01:44:05,783
Stop lying to me!

833
01:44:05,947 --> 01:44:08,177
- Where it is?
- I don't know!

834
01:44:11,489 --> 01:44:14,769
- Let him go!
- I won't ask again!

835
01:44:15,709 --> 01:44:17,179
I don't know!

836
01:44:35,762 --> 01:44:37,402
Priest Gregor!

837
01:44:41,139 --> 01:44:43,019
Do you see what I meant?

838
01:44:45,299 --> 01:44:51,129
Neither Rogatus nor anyone else
cares about your life.

839
01:44:57,543 --> 01:45:03,413
-Osman Bey is right, Gregor.
-Rogatus!

840
01:45:03,746 --> 01:45:05,846
Don't!

841
01:45:06,553 --> 01:45:08,853
Lower your dagger.

842
01:45:09,923 --> 01:45:13,923
You aren't safe here.

843
01:45:15,055 --> 01:45:17,825
You can't leave here.

844
01:45:28,562 --> 01:45:30,612
Now...

845
01:45:31,911 --> 01:45:35,771
Leave the priest.

846
01:45:42,324 --> 01:45:46,324
You were the only one I trusted!

847
01:46:28,528 --> 01:46:31,938
God damn it!

848
01:46:34,647 --> 01:46:37,987
Father Gregor.

849
01:47:12,316 --> 01:47:16,616
We are facing both Rogatus
and Kosses.

850
01:47:17,775 --> 01:47:21,775
We'll go as the old ways, Diego.

851
01:47:23,169 --> 01:47:28,439
Anselmo needs power.
Power needs gold.

852
01:47:32,867 --> 01:47:37,307
If we move right now,
we'll reach the point by the sun fall.

853
01:47:37,307 --> 01:47:40,217
And set the ambush.

854
01:47:42,361 --> 01:47:46,361
What are we waiting for, Diego?

855
01:47:46,705 --> 01:47:51,045
Tell the men to prepare.

856
01:47:51,309 --> 01:47:55,309
Come on! Get up!

857
01:47:56,773 --> 01:48:00,063
Come on!

858
01:48:09,040 --> 01:48:13,040
I still can't understand!
He was my friend...

859
01:48:18,595 --> 01:48:23,355
I'm embarrassed against you.
I didn't listen to you.

860
01:48:27,375 --> 01:48:30,865
A proverb says...

861
01:48:30,865 --> 01:48:36,025
''A calamity is better than a
thousand advises.''

862
01:48:36,025 --> 01:48:40,125
Even if I had told you a thousand times,
you wouldn't get it before seeing it.

863
01:48:41,558 --> 01:48:47,178
But you now understand that only safe
place in Bhytinia is...

864
01:48:47,907 --> 01:48:52,667
my side.
-I understand it, Osman Bey.

865
01:48:52,667 --> 01:48:56,667
Even though the truth slapped
me on my face, I do.

866
01:49:02,247 --> 01:49:06,247
I want to meet the Christian folk
in Söğüt.

867
01:49:06,247 --> 01:49:10,707
If you allow me, I want to let them
now that I'm with them now.

868
01:49:16,868 --> 01:49:20,868
Then, let's go to Söğüt.

869
01:49:58,147 --> 01:50:02,017
Bilecik Castle

870
01:50:02,017 --> 01:50:07,057
That vile priest united with
Osman and tried to test me!

871
01:50:07,057 --> 01:50:10,487
This is unbelievable!

872
01:50:12,065 --> 01:50:17,005
My friend Gregor,
if friendships are in the past...

873
01:50:17,853 --> 01:50:21,853
your life lost its value.

874
01:50:22,945 --> 01:50:28,225
Whatever he is hiding,
we'll find out.

875
01:50:30,130 --> 01:50:35,520
I have one more bad news.
While you were busy with Gregor...

876
01:50:35,520 --> 01:50:40,440
they attacked the mine!

877
01:50:44,032 --> 01:50:48,772
The mine! Osman!

878
01:50:48,772 --> 01:50:52,302
Osman!

879
01:51:24,555 --> 01:51:29,395
Priest Gregor will live
with us here now.

880
01:51:42,586 --> 01:51:45,516
My sheik.

881
01:51:47,878 --> 01:51:51,358
Priest Gregor.

882
01:51:53,788 --> 01:51:57,788
Sheik Edebali, the candle that
enlightens our paths...

883
01:51:57,788 --> 01:52:02,348
the light of the Kayı.

884
01:52:04,926 --> 01:52:08,926
Welcome, priest.

885
01:52:08,926 --> 01:52:12,926
We are delighted by your
arrivel...

886
01:52:12,926 --> 01:52:15,806
as much as the non-Muslims.

887
01:52:15,806 --> 01:52:19,806
I'm grateful for your kindness,
Sheik Edebali.

888
01:52:19,806 --> 01:52:23,476
We are happy to see you.

889
01:52:23,476 --> 01:52:29,206
We would like you to visit
our lodge soon.

890
01:52:29,440 --> 01:52:35,210
-Priest Gregor.
-Of course. So do I, Sheik Edebali.

891
01:53:02,980 --> 01:53:06,540
My sheik.

892
01:53:15,982 --> 01:53:19,512
Come, Priest Gregor.

893
01:53:57,629 --> 01:54:00,869
Good job, Diego.

894
01:54:00,869 --> 01:54:04,729
I hope they are loaded as you said.

895
01:54:06,794 --> 01:54:11,754
Don't doubt that, Leader Anselmo.

896
01:54:30,536 --> 01:54:33,866
Attack!

897
01:54:52,138 --> 01:54:57,008
If you want to survive,
give us your goods!

898
01:54:57,745 --> 01:55:00,895
Give them!

899
01:55:04,735 --> 01:55:07,735
Come on!

900
01:55:10,088 --> 01:55:14,088
That was easy.
Pleasing, isn't it?

901
01:55:20,272 --> 01:55:23,052
Haven't you heard it?

902
01:55:27,800 --> 01:55:32,420
If you want to survive,
give us your goods!

903
01:55:36,893 --> 01:55:40,493
Alps!

904
01:55:47,294 --> 01:55:50,834
It's time for revenge, Anselmo!

905
01:55:50,834 --> 01:55:54,174
So be it, Turgut.

906
01:55:54,174 --> 01:55:58,834
Let's see if you are as brave when
I'm not tied up.

907
01:55:59,482 --> 01:56:03,192
Anselmo is always brave.

908
01:56:17,114 --> 01:56:21,804
But you aren't a good swordsman
even when you are free.

909
01:56:21,804 --> 01:56:26,044
Don't speak, come at me!

910
01:56:44,008 --> 01:56:47,308
Come at me!

911
01:57:14,456 --> 01:57:18,846
I told you!
I will choke you on your gold!

912
01:57:31,904 --> 01:57:35,354
Go to hell!

913
01:57:49,262 --> 01:57:53,262
-They are retreating!
-Anselmo!

914
01:57:58,803 --> 01:58:03,563
Kutan, send the wounded to the tribe.

915
01:58:04,675 --> 01:58:08,975
We'll take their corpses
to Osman Bey.

916
01:58:08,975 --> 01:58:11,695
As you order, my bey.

917
01:58:25,570 --> 01:58:29,570
Wouldn't we be impressed...

918
01:58:29,570 --> 01:58:34,550
if we heard how the Christ
begged God...

919
01:58:34,550 --> 01:58:38,550
for unity among us...

920
01:58:38,550 --> 01:58:42,550
and unity with God?

921
01:58:48,243 --> 01:58:53,753
Now, we hear this beseeching
with our eyes from the holy book.

922
01:58:53,753 --> 01:58:57,753
The separation among our people,
rivalry...

923
01:58:57,753 --> 01:59:02,163
and the tendency for selfishness
is strong but...

924
01:59:02,163 --> 01:59:07,733
we Christians should be the agents
of unity.

925
01:59:46,709 --> 01:59:49,939
Priest Gregor!

926
01:59:50,711 --> 01:59:54,711
Priest Gregor!
Priest Gregor!

927
01:59:55,896 --> 01:59:59,436
Hang on!

928
02:00:03,591 --> 02:00:07,581
Priest Gregor!

929
02:00:08,614 --> 02:00:11,634
Priest Gregor!

930
02:00:35,066 --> 02:00:39,746
Master Gregor!
My unlucky master!

931
02:01:01,000 --> 02:01:04,700
With the name of Allah.

932
02:01:34,921 --> 02:01:38,521
-Osman Bey.
-Brother.

933
02:01:38,521 --> 02:01:40,901
My sheik.

934
02:01:42,873 --> 02:01:46,873
My bey, Baysungur is here.

935
02:01:58,987 --> 02:02:04,407
We have a word from our scouts.
We know the route of Rogatus' caravan.

936
02:03:01,276 --> 02:03:06,876
Be quick! We must reach Bilecik Castle
at once!

937
02:03:10,794 --> 02:03:14,794
Guards! Keep your eyes open!

938
02:03:32,331 --> 02:03:36,591
Alps! They'll be here soon.

939
02:03:38,247 --> 02:03:42,247
Now is the time for a clash!

940
02:03:44,274 --> 02:03:47,934
Now is the time for a slaughter!

941
02:03:47,934 --> 02:03:53,064
You'll take all the goods.
Not a single man will survive.

942
02:03:53,064 --> 02:03:56,594
As you order, my bey.

943
02:03:56,841 --> 02:03:59,171
Come on!

944
02:04:52,149 --> 02:04:55,859
Take defensive formation!

945
02:04:57,854 --> 02:05:01,574
Protect the caravan!

946
02:05:01,837 --> 02:05:05,837
God is with us!

947
02:05:11,160 --> 02:05:15,160
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

948
02:07:07,982 --> 02:07:12,932
Theodor! If God is with you...

949
02:07:13,591 --> 02:07:17,711
why are you running away like a
jackal running from a lion?

950
02:07:17,711 --> 02:07:21,711
Face me, then!
Come on!

951
02:07:54,554 --> 02:07:58,554
Come on! Come on, brothers!

952
02:08:25,734 --> 02:08:31,224
My shoulder was cut so many
times that I feel nothing now.

953
02:08:36,774 --> 02:08:41,934
When I behead you, you will feel it.

954
02:09:17,276 --> 02:09:22,716
If you don't want me to kill you,
tell me everything.

955
02:09:29,757 --> 02:09:34,937
The other caravans of your master.
Their routes.

956
02:09:35,352 --> 02:09:38,382
Their loads too.

957
02:09:39,719 --> 02:09:43,439
You will tell me everything.

958
02:09:44,752 --> 02:09:48,752
How many soldiers are waiting
at Bilecik Castle?

959
02:09:49,872 --> 02:09:53,872
How many soldiers does Rogatus have
in his villages?

960
02:09:54,662 --> 02:09:58,502
Tell me everything!

961
02:09:59,347 --> 02:10:01,827
Never.

962
02:10:06,283 --> 02:10:10,283
So, your life isn't precious?

963
02:10:10,843 --> 02:10:16,713
I won't make it easier for you, Osman Bey.

964
02:10:22,100 --> 02:10:29,020
Finally, Heaven.

965
02:10:37,431 --> 02:10:41,911
I doubt that's where you are heading.

966
02:10:53,619 --> 02:10:58,779
The only place you will go is hell!

967
02:11:49,422 --> 02:11:54,642
My bey, you didn't leave
anyone alive.

968
02:11:59,391 --> 02:12:03,391
We have the goods, my bey.

969
02:12:04,419 --> 02:12:09,859
They thought that we would give up
after they strike our trade!

970
02:12:10,931 --> 02:12:15,961
But they couldn't see the truth
because of the light of our swords!

971
02:12:16,593 --> 02:12:21,293
Now, we'll show them the truth!

972
02:12:21,992 --> 02:12:32,812
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

973
02:12:34,117 --> 02:12:39,297
Take his head.
We are going to the lords.

974
02:13:36,099 --> 02:13:47,092
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com